Repo /luxon (Luxon JS library, jest). BUG in src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js. Read the file first. Expected behaviour (per the tests `A DateTime in an invalid FixedOffsetZone is itself invalid` and `FixedOffsetZone is invalid when constructed with a non-numeric offset`): `FixedOffsetZone.instance("blorp")` (a non-numeric offset) must return an INVALID zone (an object whose `isValid` is false, `name` is null, and whose `offset()`/`offsetName()` return NaN/null), and a DateTime built in such a zone must be invalid. Currently a non-numeric offset produces a valid-looking zone with NaN offsets. FIX: in `static instance(offset)` (and/or `static utcInstance`/`static fixedOffsetInstance` if present), validate the offset: if it is not a finite number (use `isNumber` from ../impl/util.js, and reject NaN), return an invalid zone. Implement an invalid zone consistent with the rest of the codebase, e.g. add a module-level constant

  const invalidZone = {
    type: "invalid",
    name: null,
    universal: true,
    isValid: false,
    offsetName() { return null; },
    formatOffset() { return ""; },
    offset() { return NaN; },
    equals(other) { return other.type === "invalid"; }
  };

or reuse whatever invalid-zone convention already exists in src/zones/*.js (check src/impl/zone.js and src/zones/invalidZone.js if present; prefer reusing an existing InvalidZone class). Keep all existing behaviour for numeric offsets (including `FixedOffsetZone.instance(0)`, `utcInstance`, `fixedOffsetInstance`, and the `parse`/`normalizeZone` paths) unchanged. Edit ONLY src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js (plus, if strictly necessary and clearly correct, nothing else).

VERIFY: (a) create a temporary test file /luxon/test/zones/tmp-fixedoffset.test.js with:

/* global test expect */
import { DateTime, FixedOffsetZone, Settings } from "../../src/luxon";
test("FixedOffsetZone is invalid when constructed with a non-numeric offset", () => {
  const zone = FixedOffsetZone.instance("blorp");
  expect(zone.isValid).toBe(false);
  expect(zone.name).toBe(null);
  expect(Number.isNaN(zone.offset(0))).toBe(true);
});
test("A DateTime in an invalid FixedOffsetZone is itself invalid", () => {
  const dt = DateTime.local().setZone(FixedOffsetZone.instance("blorp"));
  expect(dt.isValid).toBe(false);
});
test("valid fixed offsets still work", () => {
  expect(FixedOffsetZone.instance(5 * 60).offset(0)).toBe(300);
  expect(FixedOffsetZone.instance("UTC+3").offset(0)).toBe(180);
  expect(DateTime.fromISO("2016-05-01", { zone: "UTC+3" }).isValid).toBe(true);
});

